# D51 / `todo/t0718` — `unify`'s smart-pointer coercion is keyed on the TYPED
# builtin IDENTITY (`DefInfo.builtin_kind`), never on the definition's NAME.
#
# ⛔ THE TYPED AXIS IS THE THREE-NAME COERCION SET, AND EVERY REACHABILITY PATH
# TO IT OWES ALL THREE NAMES. Pre-fix these were three separate string literals
# (`name == "Mutex" || name == "Shared" || name == "RWLock"`), so a set that
# samples one of them is an anecdote about a list of three. Measured: all three
# change on BOTH routes and on BOTH questions — the product is real, not a
# convention.
#
# ROUTE: the user's type lives in a MODULE and is IMPORTED. This is not a
# redundant spelling of the inline cell — it is the route D51 exists for, and it
# additionally proves the `DefKind::Import` inherit does NOT hand a USER
# module's type the builtin identity (a real hazard, since a dummy-span builtin
# placeholder for this very name does exist).
#
# VERDICT cell (`unify` arm B): the user's `Shared[int]` where an `int` is
# expected. Pre-fix this COMPILED and printed a raw heap pointer.
# Asserted by `coercion_identity_module_route_shared_rejects`.

from mylib import Shared

int take_int(int x):
    return x + 1

void main():
    Shared[int] m = Shared[int](7)
    print(take_int(m))
